[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug: the parser reads dates month first. The reports it
merged hold three problems, with three different fixes. Fixing the parser closes only the
first one.

<Callout kind="warn">
Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: `parser` fixed (fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales),
`hint` won't fix (booking-v3 form retired). `shift` was in neither: it is still open.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<SplitTable ticket={4471} repo="karol1on/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows" issues={{ parser: 1, hint: 2, shift: 3 }} />

Counts are unique report ids: the ticket export repeats some rows across its pages.

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** Every tenant on file writes the
day first. A booking for 7 April goes out for 4 July. Reports arrive by app and email, and by
booking-v2's form, whose hint says `DD/MM/YYYY`.

**`hint`: booking-v3's form tells people to type the month first.** Its hint says
`MM/DD/YYYY`, then the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. Only tenants on
booking-v3, only through the form. The parser fix does not touch it: the form needs the right
hint for the tenant's locale.

**`shift`: the day moves by one, not month and day.** "Lisbon got Tuesday, Toronto got Monday",
"every booking in June is one day off", "the invite arrived before I made the booking". That is
a time zone or daylight-saving bug, not date order. The desk had already read these reports
as a one-day move (desk notes). The table counts them where they are filed, under `parser`,
and again on their own row.

## How it got merged

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line. "Wrong day on
  the invite" fits all three problems, so all three landed in one ticket.
- Intake tags by the reporter's browser, not by the tenant and form. The tags in the table
  disagree with the cause in both directions; go by tenant and channel.

## For the desk

- Route new date reports by tenant, form and channel (`#lib/kb/causes`), not by subject or tag.
- A report that says "one day off" is `shift`, whatever its subject. Add its id to
  `oneDayMove` in desk notes.

